    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Calculate the gradient of the interval joining $A(-2,6)$ and $B(4,-3)$.",
        "solution_text": "Use $(x_1,y_1)=(-2,6)$ and $(x_2,y_2)=(4,-3)$.\n\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\\\&=\\dfrac{-3-6}{4-(-2)}\\\\&=\\dfrac{-9}{6}\\\\&=-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe interval falls from left to right, matching the negative gradient.\n\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.5cm,y=0.5cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\definecolor{gradientBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\definecolor{gradientRed}{HTML}{EF6068}\n\\draw[thick,gradientBlue] (-2,6)--(4,-3);\n\\draw[dashed,gradientRed] (-2,6)--(4,6)--(4,-3);\n\\draw[black] (3.5,6)--(3.5,5.5)--(4,5.5);\n\\fill[black] (-2,6) circle (2pt);\n\\fill[black] (4,-3) circle (2pt);\n\\path (-2,6) node[left] {$A(-2,6)$};\n\\path (4,-3) node[below] {$B(4,-3)$};\n\\path (1,6) node[above] {run $=6$};\n\\path (4,1.5) node[right] {rise $=-9$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Calculate the gradient of the interval joining $A(-3,2)$ and $B(5,2)$.\n\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\definecolor{gradientBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\draw[thick,gradientBlue] (0,0)--(4,0);\n\\fill[black] (0,0) circle (2pt);\n\\fill[black] (4,0) circle (2pt);\n\\path (0,0) node[above] {$A(-3,2)$};\n\\path (4,0) node[above] {$B(5,2)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\\\&=\\dfrac{2-2}{5-(-3)}\\\\&=\\dfrac{0}{8}\\\\&=0\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe rise is $0$ and the run is $8$, so the horizontal interval has gradient $0$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Calculate the gradient of the interval joining $A(1,-4)$ and $B(1,3)$.\n\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\definecolor{gradientBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\draw[thick,gradientBlue] (0,0)--(0,3.5);\n\\fill[black] (0,0) circle (2pt);\n\\fill[black] (0,3.5) circle (2pt);\n\\path (0,0) node[right] {$A(1,-4)$};\n\\path (0,3.5) node[right] {$B(1,3)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\\\&=\\dfrac{3-(-4)}{1-1}\\\\&=\\dfrac{7}{0}\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe rise is $7$ and the run is $0$. Division by $0$ is undefined, so the vertical interval has an **undefined** gradient."
      }
    ],
